{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310828,"nonce":"GWdUE9bMUc6Yg09f+6qYHQZsejA=","title":"nue.chat Conversation API (arch-aware) + THE compiler fix for interface-method-returns-object SIGSEGV (spurious unbox of raw iface-call ...","message":"Long-context llama-chat was: crashing (`KVCache overflow: 4097 \u003e 4096`), incoherent (repetition loops), slow/too-long. All fixed, PLUS a real compiler fix that the user pushed for (\"WE KEEP PATCHING INSTEAD OF PERMANENTLY FIXING\").\n\n**Root:** TAST erases an interface method's return type to `Dynamic` cross-module (W0014 \"cross-context iface return resolved late\"). MIR recovers the concrete type into `interface_call_result_types` (register→TypeId), but the recovery arrived too late for the box/unbox coercions. So `var logits:Tensor = model.forwardIds(ids)` (model: an interface) saw a `Dynamic` source → target `Tensor` and inserted an **unbox**, reading a *raw* Tensor pointer as a box header → SIGSEGV. Object returns crashed; scalar (Int) returns silently corrupted.\n\n**Fix (all in hir_to_mir.rs, ~80 lines), each keyed on `interface_call_result_types.get(\u0026reg)`:**\n1. **Let coercion (~4879):** `init_ty = interface_call_result_types.get(value_reg).unwrap_or(init_expr.ty)`; use `init_ty` in maybe_box_value/maybe_unbox_value/optional/abstract. Direct `var x = iface.m()` fixed.\n2. **var_type (~4888):** `type_hint.or(Some(init_ty))` not `init_expr.ty` — inferred bindings infer the recovered type, not Dynamic (else scalar returns get spuriously boxed).\n3. **Ternary/if-expr phi (`lower_conditional_typed` ~31896):** if both arms are tracked iface results with the SAME real_ty, insert the phi result into `interface_call_result_types`. Fixes `cond ? iface.a() : iface.b()` (the prefill `useFastLastLogits() ? forwardLastLogits : forwardIds`). Require agreement so mixed merges aren't mislabelled.\n4. **Assignment coercion (~5317):** same `rhs_ty` recovery for reassignment `logits = model.forwardLastLogits(...)` (decode loop). Different code path from Let.\n5. **Scalar guard (~4860):** don't set `var_concrete_overrides` for scalar recovered types (it's for object dispatch only). Principled; did NOT fix the scalar-inferred bug below.\n\n**Validated** on minimal cross-module repro `/tmp/ifacetest` (interface in pkg `model`, consumer in pkg `gen`): direct/ternary/reassign object returns all correct; nue llama+qwen coherent end-to-end with `GenerationLoop`/`SpeculativeGenerationLoop`/`Conversation` all typed on `nue.CausalLanguageModel` (NO downcast). Two rebuild lessons: (a) ALWAYS `find /tmp/... -name .rayzor -exec rm -rf` between edited-source runs (stale cache gave inverted pass/fail); (b) iterate compiler fixes on a ~40-line repro (`rayzor run Main.hx --llvm --release`, ~2s), not the full bundle+model.\n\n**OPEN follow-up:** inferred scalar iface-return used DIRECTLY (`var c = iface.count(); return c;` or `if (c\u003e0)`) still returns garbage — annotate `:Int` (works, S2) or use in arithmetic (`c+0`, works, S3). Fix #2/#5 didn't resolve it; deeper than var_concrete_overrides — suspect the symbol's local-type registration after the Let coercion. GenerationLoop's `var _cacheCap:Int = model.cacheCapacity()` is annotated to sidestep.\n\n**Interface contract:** added `cacheLen()`/`cacheCapacity()`/`rewindCache()` to `nue.CausalLanguageModel` (LlamaModel already implements). Only LlamaModel implements it, so expanding was safe.\n\n`nue/nue/chat/`: `Message` (role:String open set), `ChatTemplate` (kind:String tag; Llama3 header vs ChatML vs Raw; `forModel(arch:Architecture, tok)` picks by registered specials then arch), `GenerationConfig` (maxNewTokens/temperature/repetitionPenalty=1.3/topK/seed/useSpeculative + greedy()/balanced()/creative()/copy()), `ChatResponse` (text + promptTokens + completionTokens + `FinishReason` enum Stop/Length/ContextFull/Aborted/Unknown), `Conversation` (system()/addUser/ask()→ChatResponse/askSilent/reset/nextPrompt). `nue/nue/model/Architecture.hx`: closed enum Llama/Qwen2/Mistral/… + `Architectures.fromString/toName` (metadata.architecture stays String = open ArchRegistry key). Loops report `finishReason:String` + honor `stopIds:Array\u003cInt\u003e` (multi-stop). Main.hx consumes Conversation (deleted hand-rolled Llama-only template + sampler + eos). Follow-up: promote ChatTemplate.kind/Message.role String tags to enums once comfortable.\n\n- **KVCache overflow crash:** `GenerationLoop` decode loop had NO context bound (only EOS + maxNewTokens); maxtok 5000 \u003e ctx 4096 → throw at 4097. Added `cacheCapacity()` accessor + `if (cacheLen()+1 \u003e cap) { finishReason=\"context\"; break; }` before the forward. Stops cleanly (finish=context).\n- **Incoherence:** `repPenalty` default was `1.0` (OFF) despite the comment saying \"Default 1.3\" — run_bundle.sh never passed arg[5]. → 1.0 let the 1B model loop (\"In conclusion… In conclusion…\"). Fixed default to 1.3 (Main.hx) + run_bundle.sh exposes `REP_PENALTY=1.3`. Voronoi prompt: 10 loops → 0.\n- **Qwen ChatML stop token:** GGUFTokenizer registered `tokenizer.ggml.eos_token_id` under the hardcoded Llama name `\u003c|end_of_text|\u003e`, so Qwen's real eos (151645 `\u003c|im_end|\u003e`) was unnamed and lookups missed → eos=-1, ran past turn into hallucinated turns. Fix: added `\u003c|im_start|\u003e`,`\u003c|im_end|\u003e`,`\u003c|endoftext|\u003e` to the `chatSpecials` vocab-lookup list (same pattern as Llama-3 specials). Qwen now eos=151645, finish=stop.\n- **Defaults:** run_bundle.sh MAX_TOKENS 5000→1024.\n\nPeak ~2.95GB is model weights + KV cache preallocated to ctx=4096 (~537MB Q8 for Llama-1B), NOT the leak. The *unbounded climb* (ran to 5000 tok then crashed) is FIXED by the context bound. Residual per-token leak (~390KB/tok, [[bugs_pool_data_flow_gap]]) persists but is now bounded by ctx. Lower CTX to shrink base.\n\nFeedback reinforced: user HATES compiler/runtime-limitation narration in Nue docs (stale, forgotten) — scrubbed from Architecture/Message/ChatTemplate/LlamaModel.parameters. Test compiler fixes on SMALL repros. [[project_qwen2_and_tensor_plugin_migration]] [[feedback_nue_drives_compiler_fixes]]\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_conversation_api_and_iface_return_fix` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}